.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt FBCOMPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fbcompd
.Nd simple framebuffer compositor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar font
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is a small compositor that draws client windows on the
framebuffer
.Pa /dev/fb0 .
It is a proof of concept and predates
.Xr wlcompd 8 .
It does not speak Wayland.
.Pp
Clients connect to the
.Ux Ns -domain
stream socket
.Pa /tmp/fbcompd.sock .
Each client draws its window into a System V shared-memory segment and
sends the segment ID to
.Nm .
The protocol is defined in
.In fbcomp_proto.h .
Every message is one fixed-size
.Vt struct fbc_msg .
.Pp
.Nm
serves at most 16 clients and 16 windows.
A window may be at most 4096 by 4096 pixels.
.Nm
copies the pixels from the segment only when the client commits, so a
client that is still drawing cannot tear the picture.
When a client goes away,
.Nm
removes its shared-memory segment.
.Pp
The optional
.Ar font
argument is the path of a TrueType font used for titles.
If it is not given, the font named by
.Ev FBCOMPD_FONT
is used, and then
.Pa /usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSansMono.ttf .
If the font cannot be loaded, windows have no title text.
.Pp
.Nm
does not detach from the terminal.
.Ss Windows
Each window has a title bar with its title and three boxes at the
right end: minimize, maximize and close.
A resize grip is drawn in the bottom-right corner.
The topmost window that is not minimized has the keyboard focus and a
brighter title bar.
.Pp
Only the left mouse button is used.
.Bl -bullet
.It
A click on a window raises it.
.It
Dragging the title bar moves the window.
Moving a maximized window ends the maximized state.
.It
The close box tells the client its window is closed and removes it.
.It
The maximize box makes the window fill the screen, or restores its old
size and position.
.It
The minimize box hides the window and puts a button for it on a
taskbar along the bottom of the screen.
A click on that button restores the window.
The taskbar is only shown while a window is minimized.
.It
Dragging the resize grip asks the client to reallocate its window at the
new size.
The smallest size is 80 by 48 pixels.
.It
A click inside a window is passed to its client, with the position
relative to the window.
.El
.Ss Keyboard
Key presses and releases go to the focused window.
Each key event carries the USB HID key code, an ASCII character for keys
on a US layout, and the state of the Shift, Control and Alt keys.
The modifier keys themselves are not sent.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width FBCOMPD_FONT
.It Ev FBCOMPD_FONT
Path of the title font, used if no
.Ar font
argument is given.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSansMono.ttf -compact
.It Pa /dev/fb0
The framebuffer.
.It Pa /dev/kbdmux
The keyboard.
.Pa /dev/kbd0
is tried if it cannot be opened.
.It Pa /dev/mousemux
The mouse.
.Pa /dev/mouse0
is tried if it cannot be opened.
.It Pa /tmp/fbcompd.sock
The listening socket.
Any old socket is removed at start-up.
.It Pa /tmp/COMP
The log.
It is truncated at start-up.
If it cannot be created, the log goes to standard output.
.It Pa /usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSansMono.ttf
The default title font.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/fbcompd
Starts
.Nm
at boot when
.Va fbcompd
is set to
.Dq YES
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Va fbcompd_flags
is passed as arguments, so it can name a font.
The process ID is recorded in
.Pa /var/run/fbcompd.pid .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 if it cannot open the framebuffer or set up its socket.
It exits 0 if
.Xr select 2
fails.
Otherwise it runs until it is killed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wlclient 1 ,
.Xr select 2 ,
.Xr shmget 2 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr minix-service 8 ,
.Xr wlcompd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
daemon first appeared in Ixolo 0.1.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
and
.Xr wlcompd 8
must not run at the same time.
Both use the framebuffer and the keyboard.
.Pp
While
.Nm
holds
.Pa /dev/kbdmux ,
the console no longer receives keyboard input.
.Sh BUGS
Only the left mouse button is supported, and only presses are passed to
clients.
Mouse motion and releases are not.
.Pp
The ASCII translation knows only a US keyboard layout.
